body:
Moves UberBond's recursive self-completion heartbeat onto the sovereign local authoring node.

What changes:
- authoring cadence drops from 15 minutes to one minute after each completed pulse (`OnUnitInactiveSec=60s`, 10s boot wake, 1s accuracy, zero randomized delay);
- verified local promotions and founder intents still wake the same authoring service immediately through existing systemd path units;
- `uberbond-authorctl wake` now runs a new sovereign continuous authoring pulse;
- finite-completion work retains absolute priority;
- when exact-current finite engineering is genuinely closed, the local pulse invokes the already-canonical Sandwich Autocatalytic Governor and emits one bounded descendant-genesis `LOCAL_PREPARATION` task;
- the same OS-separated local worker, verifier, promoter and post-promotion wake chain handles the fold;
- the continuation receipt uses the same digest algorithm/schema as the mature local autonomy pulse so minute/event reentry resumes an existing attempt rather than spawning duplicates;
- a worker inbox already bound to another task fails closed rather than being overwritten;
- no Vercel, GitHub Actions schedule, ChatGPT automation, or cloud cron is required for this heartbeat.

Added hostile tests for minute cadence, event wakes, finite-priority, cloud-independent descendant task creation, digest-bound local dispatch, same-attempt resume, and worker-inbox collision refusal.

Truth boundary: source readiness does not prove a physical sovereign node is installed/running. Continuous real-world execution still requires an owner-controlled always-on Linux node plus a configured local model/runtime. This change adds no merge/sign/deploy/spend/customer/payment/credential/DNS authority.

