Replaces the sovereign authoring brain's 15-minute periodic timer with a resident owner-controlled systemd continuum and moves Sandwich descendant-genesis into the local pulse itself.

Core behavior:
- resident `uberbond-authoring-continuum.service` starts on boot and stays alive;
- each truth-first authoring pulse runs to completion, then the next starts after 60 seconds;
- systemd restarts the continuum after process failure;
- continuum has `PrivateNetwork=true` and AF_UNIX-only networking, so its heartbeat has no Vercel/GitHub/hosted scheduler dependency;
- every resident/manual/founder-intent/post-promotion wake serializes through one local `flock`, preventing overlapping authoring brains;
- installer disables/removes the legacy `uberbond-authoring.timer` and enables the resident continuum;
- readiness/doctor now require the continuum and explicitly report `hostedSchedulerRequiredForSelfCompletion=false`;
- when exact-current finite engineering is closed, the local pulse no longer sleeps: it compiles one Sandwich descendant-genesis task locally and feeds the existing isolated worker -> verifier -> promoter conveyor;
- requirement genesis remains separate from implementation, and same-base continuation policy still prevents duplicate attempts.

Truth boundary: this is source-level cloud-independent continuous self-completion machinery. Actual 24/7/minute operation is not claimed until installed and observed on owner-controlled Linux hardware with an attested local model and the existing verifier/promoter path. No customer/payment/physical/life/ASI proof is created.

