## Truth boundary
This makes the source-side direct communication surface materially usable and conversational. It does not prove physical availability. The Center becomes reachable only after an owner-controlled Linux founder node and owner-supplied local model runtime/model artifacts are activated. The final iPad address is the founder node's private RFC1918 address on port 8787, protected by the generated founder token.

## Defect
The founder wrapper was hardened in #653, but the direct offline llama installer still resolved the owner-supplied llama-server and GGUF paths with `realpath` before checking `! -L`. A direct invocation could therefore erase symlink identity before admission checks.

## Repair
- validate required commands before any `realpath` use;
- preserve raw binary/model input paths;
- refuse binary and GGUF symlink aliases before path resolution;
- revalidate the resolved artifacts afterward;
- preserve checksum binding, localhost-only runtime posture, transactional rollback, zero cloud seed calls, and zero downstream business/external authority.

